  "extract": "Carl Linnaeus, also known after ennoblement in 1761 as Carl von Linné, was a Swedish biologist and physician who formalised binomial nomenclature, the modern system of naming organisms. He is known as the \"father of modern taxonomy\". Many of his writings were in Latin; his name is rendered in Latin as Carolus Linnæus and, after his 1761 ennoblement, as Carolus a Linné.",
  "extract_html": "<p><b>Carl Linnaeus</b>, also known after ennoblement in 1761 as <b>Carl von Linné</b>, was a Swedish biologist and physician who formalised binomial nomenclature, the modern system of naming organisms. He is known as the \"father of modern taxonomy\". Many of his writings were in Latin; his name is rendered in Latin as <b><span><span style=\"font-style:normal\">Carolus Linnæus</span></span></b> and, after his 1761 ennoblement, as <b><span><span style=\"font-style:normal\">Carolus a Linné</span></span></b>.</p>"
